**What changed:** In zoneless change detection, `ChangeDetectionSchedulerImpl` previously switched from the macrotask to the microtask scheduler only when the scheduler itself triggered the tick. Now `switchToMicrotaskScheduler()` runs after **any** `ApplicationRef.tick`, including ticks triggered directly (most notably during bootstrap) (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/06be8034bb9b9adfc07ab0d40cd87c6ae5de02de). This keeps promises scheduled during synchronization — e.g. `Promise.resolve().then(() => updateAppStateAgain())`, as used by `NgModel` — within the same event loop so they aren't split across multiple browser paints. The change adds a `taskService.add()` around the `appRef.afterTick` handling and moves `this.taskService.remove(task)` into the `finally` block of the scheduler tick. Exemptions: ticks when ZoneJS is present (`!this.zonelessEnabled`) and test-initiated ticks via `TestBed.tick` / `ComponentFixture.detectChanges` (detected through the now-internal `includeAllTestViews` flag on `ApplicationRef`), so `fixture.whenStable` timing is unchanged. A direct `ApplicationRef.tick()` from application-under-test code still gets microtask treatment. Fixes issue #65444: `<mat-checkbox [ngModel]="true">` flickering on initial load in zoneless mode (https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/65444).

**Affects:** Zoneless (`provideZonelessChangeDetection` / no ZoneJS) Angular 21 applications that call `ApplicationRef.tick()` directly (including bootstrap's initial tick), and tests whose stability assertions depend on timing after such a tick. ZoneJS-based apps and `TestBed.tick`/`ComponentFixture.detectChanges`-driven tests are unaffected.

**Action:** required: re-verify initial-render behavior of `ngModel`-bound controls (e.g. `mat-checkbox`, `mat-slide-toggle`) in zoneless apps, and re-verify any code that calls `ApplicationRef.tick()` manually or asserts on `ApplicationRef.isStable` / `whenStable` immediately after a tick — stability may now lag by one microtask.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// afterTick handling in ChangeDetectionSchedulerImpl (21.1)
if (!this.runningTick) {
  this.cleanup();
  // Ticks when ZoneJS is present or initiated from tests do not get
  // the microtask scheduling treatment.
  if (!this.zonelessEnabled || this.appRef.includeAllTestViews) {
    this.taskService.remove(task);
    return;
  }
}
this.switchToMicrotaskScheduler();
this.taskService.remove(task);
```

**What changed:** `providePlatformInitializer` in `@angular/core` now returns `StaticProvider` instead of `EnvironmentProviders`. Previously it wrapped the provider in `makeEnvironmentProviders([...])`, producing a type that could not be passed to APIs taking `StaticProvider[]`, so `platformBrowser([providePlatformInitializer(() => {})])` failed with `TS2322: Type EnvironmentProviders is not assignable to type StaticProvider` (issue #64277). The function now returns the plain provider `{ provide: PLATFORM_INITIALIZER, useValue: initializerFn, multi: true }` (commit b4f584cf42235c94bb8389fa55bc634e23d7b010, https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/b4f584cf42235c94bb8389fa55bc634e23d7b010; https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/64277). The docs also add a usage note showing the intended pattern: create the platform via `platformBrowser([providePlatformInitializer(...)])` and pass it as `platformRef` to `bootstrapApplication` (same commit).

**Affects:** Applications calling `providePlatformInitializer` — e.g. code that cast/worked around the old `EnvironmentProviders` return type, or code passing its result where a `StaticProvider` is required (platform creation such as `platformBrowser(...)` / `createOrReusePlatformInjector(...)`).

**Action:** none — the fix only widens compatibility; existing calls that passed the result to environment/`ɵcreateOrReusePlatformInjector` paths via `as any` casts can drop the cast, and initializers should now be passed directly to platform creation (`platformBrowser([...])` with `bootstrapApplication(App, appConfig, { platformRef })`). Re-verify that platform initializers still run exactly once per platform.

**Before/after:**
```typescript
// Before (21.0): returns EnvironmentProviders — not assignable to StaticProvider
const platform = platformBrowser([
  providePlatformInitializer(() => {}), // TS2322: Type EnvironmentProviders is not assignable to type StaticProvider
]);

// After (21.1): returns StaticProvider
export function providePlatformInitializer(initializerFn: () => void): StaticProvider;

const platformRef = platformBrowser([providePlatformInitializer(() => { /* ... */ })]);
bootstrapApplication(App, appConfig, { platformRef });
```

**What changed:** In `@angular/forms/signals`, `FieldState` gained a new method `focusBoundControl(): void` — "Focuses the first UI control in the DOM that is bound to this field state. If no UI control is bound, does nothing." (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/angular/angular/1ea5c97703ad3c6d8e4cb1b4297eec57629ce117/packages/forms/signals/src/api/types.ts). Implementation: `FieldNode.focusBoundControl()` calls `this.getBindingForFocus()?.focus()`, preferring focusable bindings on the field itself and otherwise the first focusable binding among descendant fields, resolved by DOM order (`firstInDom`, `Node.DOCUMENT_POSITION_PRECEDING`) (…/packages/forms/signals/src/field/node.ts). The `FormField<T>` directive gained an optional public `focus?(): void`; the core render3 control instruction was refactored, exporting `ɵFormFieldDirective` and `ɵCustomControl` instead of `ɵControl` from `@angular/core` private exports and adding `customControlIndex`/`getCustomControl` wiring so native, custom (`value`/`checked`), and interop controls can be focused (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/1ea5c97703ad3c6d8e4cb1b4297eec57629ce117).

**Affects:** Applications using signal forms (`form()`, `FieldTree`/`FieldState`) that want programmatic focus; no existing behavior removed. Only apps that implemented the `FieldState` interface by hand would see a new required member; only consumers of `ɵControl` from `@angular/core` private exports see renames.

**Action:** none (purely additive API). Custom classes implementing `FieldState` must add `focusBoundControl(): void`; apps relying on the private `ɵControl` export must move to `ɵFormFieldDirective`.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// new in FieldState (goldens/public-api/forms/signals/index.api.md)
focusBoundControl(): void;

// new in FormField<T>
focus?(): void;

// old core private export
export {ɵCONTROL, ɵControl, ɵFieldState, ɵInteropControl} from './render3/interfaces/control';
// new
export {ɵCONTROL, ɵFieldState, ɵFormFieldDirective, ɵInteropControl} from './render3/interfaces/control';
```

